  "name": "orb",
  "description": "In-house catch orb (original design): a glossy teal-to-indigo sphere lit from the upper left, with a cyan rim, ringed at a tilt by a gold C (the Conductor C) that opens on the right, where its upper end carries a latch. No band across the sphere, no button, no red. Each row is a string, one palette key per pixel; '_' is transparent. 'closed' (16x13) waits, is thrown and is flown as a message; 'spinFront' and 'spinLeft' are the C turned so its opening faces the front and the left (closed, spinFront, spinLeft is the ring spinning); 'open' (20x16) is the sphere split along the ring's tilt, its upper part lifted with light pouring out between, the ring loosened round it. Every frame rests on the ground by its bottom row and is centred on the same x; the open frame's centre is in its light.",
